WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.984
Sjekka is built by one developer, and an AI.

00:00:03.984 --> 00:00:04.880
This is how.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.038
Haakon decides what to build.

00:00:07.038 --> 00:00:10.031
Claude Code, an AI coding agent, does the engineering:

00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:14.300
it reads the code, writes the change and its tests, and opens a pull request.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.989
Most changes start as a single sentence.

00:00:16.989 --> 00:00:20.037
Grocery list that auto checks what store is the cheapest.

00:00:20.037 --> 00:00:22.550
That became the shopping list, built overnight.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.537
Over seventy pull requests.

00:00:24.537 --> 00:00:25.921
Nearly five hundred tests.

00:00:25.921 --> 00:00:27.890
Almost every line of the app covered.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.296
Every change takes the same road.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.772
A branch, a pull request, then the pipeline.

00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:38.228
The linters and every test, including real browser and accessibility tests, run across all cores.

00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:41.660
At the same time, the Docker image is built and smoke tested.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.998
Only when both pass does it ship.

00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:46.814
The server gets a key that can do exactly one thing.

00:00:46.814 --> 00:00:50.768
It starts the new version, and rolls back on its own if it isn't healthy.

00:00:50.768 --> 00:00:53.260
From merge to production in under two minutes.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:59.880
The site sits behind a Cloudflare tunnel, so the server has no open ports, and the database is backed up every night.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.056
The AI doesn't get free rein.

00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:04.804
It can't touch the production server or its data.

00:01:04.804 --> 00:01:06.598
Merging needs Haakon's go-ahead.

00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:09.850
And every bug fix comes with a test that fails without it.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.874
AI tests the product too.

00:01:11.874 --> 00:01:19.301
In one overnight run, five personas, from a student on a phone to a senior on an iPad, walked through a copy of the real data.

00:01:19.301 --> 00:01:20.597
Fifty-two screenshots.

00:01:20.597 --> 00:01:21.541
Six root causes.

00:01:21.541 --> 00:01:22.130
Six fixes.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.093
It looks for root causes, not symptoms.

00:01:25.093 --> 00:01:28.125
Pizza had its prices split across three products:

00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:30.477
Grandiosa, Pizza Grandiosa, and Pizza.

00:01:30.477 --> 00:01:32.890
One change gave every product one name.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.076
And everything is written down.

00:01:35.076 --> 00:01:39.510
Every decision, every prompt, and every mistake the AI made, in one public document.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.942
Even this film is made by code.

00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:45.280
The script, the voice, the music edit, and every frame.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.016
One developer.

00:01:47.016 --> 00:01:47.534
One AI.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:48.940
Shipping every day.
